IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`

-- je21-schedule1: Schedule 1 (Powers to revise Jersey legislation) and Article 15(6) and (7) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021).
--
-- Schedule 1 lists, as paragraphs (a) to (q), the powers of the Law Revision Board in preparing a revision under Article 15.
-- The Board may certify a draft revision as revised legislation "only if it is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1" (15(7)).
-- The Principal Legislative Drafter must submit the draft with a statement of the changes made (other than editorial changes) and "the power relied on as authority for the change" (15(6)).
--
-- The encoding follows the brief: each change in the draft is tagged, as an input, with the power relied on, a paragraph of Schedule 1 or an editorial change of Article 14(1).
-- Whether a change really falls within the paragraph relied on (for instance whether words "appear necessary or proper" under (h), or "obsolete or redundant" under (k)) is a judgement of the Board's, and is not computed here.
-- The functions test the thing the statute makes checkable: that each change names a power, and that the power is one of those lists.
--
-- Article 15(10) lets the States amend Schedule 1 by Regulations.
-- The Table of Legislation History in the endnotes records no such amendment, and the paragraphs below are the text as deposited.

§ `Schedule 1 -- Powers to revise Jersey legislation`

-- Answers: is the power relied on one that Schedule 1 or Article 14 gives?
-- Every paragraph (a) to (q) of Schedule 1 is a power the Principal Legislative Drafter may use in preparing a revision (Article 15(4)), and so is every editorial change in Article 14(1), which Article 15(5) lets the revision use.
-- A change that names no power relies on neither.
-- src:154 | (4) The Principal Legislative Drafter may prepare in draft a revision of any Jersey legislation in accordance with any of the powers set out in Schedule 1.
-- src:155 | (5) The powers in Article 14 may also be used for the preparation of the revision.
-- src:227 | In preparing a revision under Article 15 the Law Revision Board has the power –
-- src:228 | (a) to amend the citation provision, long title, short title, words of enactment or preamble of any legislation;
-- src:229 | (b) to consolidate or split any legislation or relocate a provision into different legislation where the provision more properly belongs;
-- src:230 | (c) to rearrange the provisions of any legislation or any list in a provision of any legislation;
-- src:231 | (d) to add a table of contents or destinations to any legislation;
-- src:232 | (e) to add a heading to a provision of any legislation that does not have one and alter any heading to a provision or part of any legislation;
-- src:233 | (f) to omit any map, picture, drawing, diagram or other object;
-- src:234 | (g) to change any reference to a person, office, body, place or thing to reflect a change of name, transfer of function or provision for construction of the reference;
-- src:235 | (h) to make any adaptations and amendments that may appear necessary or proper as a consequence of constitutional or other changes in Jersey or any other place or territory or in or to any body or organisation outside Jersey;
-- src:236 | (i) to change any words to make them gender neutral;
-- src:237 | (j) to change expressions of date, money, number, time and units of measurement;
-- src:238 | (k) to delete any obsolete or redundant words or provisions;
-- src:239 | (l) to alter any words to secure uniformity of expression in any legislation;
-- src:240 | (m) to shorten any phrase or sentence;
-- src:241 | (n) to change the wording for the better application of plain language principles;
-- src:242 | (o) to add numbering to or renumber any provision;
-- src:243 | (p) to substitute for a reference to any legislation or provision of any legislation that has been re-enacted or replaced, whether with or without modifications, a reference to the legislation or provision re-enacting or replacing it; and
-- src:244 | (q) to do all other things that appear to the Board to be necessary to render revised legislation consistent with current drafting practice.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(4) and (5) and Schedule 1 (src:154-155, src:227-244)
GIVEN authority IS AN `Authority relied on for a change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` authority MEANS
    CONSIDER authority
    WHEN `a power in Schedule 1` power
        THEN CONSIDER power
            WHEN `Schedule 1(a): to amend the citation provision, long title, short title, words of enactment or preamble` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(b): to consolidate or split legislation, or relocate a provision into different legislation` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(c): to rearrange the provisions of legislation, or a list in a provision` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(d): to add a table of contents or destinations` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(e): to add a heading to a provision that has none, or alter a heading` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(f): to omit any map, picture, drawing, diagram or other object` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(g): to change a reference to reflect a change of name, transfer of function or provision for construction` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(h): to make adaptations and amendments that appear necessary or proper as a consequence of constitutional or other changes` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(i): to change words to make them gender neutral` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(j): to change expressions of date, money, number, time and units of measurement` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(k): to delete obsolete or redundant words or provisions` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(l): to alter words to secure uniformity of expression` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(m): to shorten a phrase or sentence` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(n): to change the wording for the better application of plain language principles` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(o): to add numbering to, or renumber, a provision` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(p): to substitute a reference to legislation that has been re-enacted or replaced` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `Schedule 1(q): to do all other things that appear to the Board to be necessary to render revised legislation consistent with current drafting practice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a power in Article 14` change THEN TRUE
    WHEN `no power is stated` THEN FALSE

§ `Article 15(6) and (7) -- The statement and the certification`

-- Answers: does the statement name a power for every change in it?
-- Article 15(6): the draft revision is accompanied by a statement setting out the changes made (other than editorial changes) and the power relied on as authority for the change.
-- src:156 | (6) The Principal Legislative Drafter must submit the draft revision to the other members of the Law Revision Board accompanied by a statement setting out the changes made (other than editorial changes) and the power relied on as authority for the change.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(6) (src:156)
GIVEN changes IS A LIST OF `Change in a draft revision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 15(6): the statement names a power for every change` changes MEANS
    all (GIVEN change YIELD NOT (change's `the authority relied on` EQUALS `no power is stated`)) changes

-- Answers: are all the changes made within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1?
-- Each change names a power relied on, and that power is one of those the Law gives.
-- A draft revision with no change in it has all its changes within the powers, vacuously.
-- src:157 | (7) The Law Revision Board may certify the draft revision as revised legislation only if it is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(7) (src:157)
GIVEN changes IS A LIST OF `Change in a draft revision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 15(7): all the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` changes MEANS
    all (GIVEN change YIELD `Schedule 1 and Article 14: the power relied on is one the Law gives` (change's `the authority relied on`)) changes

-- Answers: is certification open to the Law Revision Board?
-- The Board "may certify the draft revision as revised legislation only if it is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1".
-- Satisfaction is the Board's state of mind and is the one condition the paragraph states.
-- The paragraph does not say what follows if the Board is satisfied wrongly, and the model does not add that.
-- src:157 | (7) The Law Revision Board may certify the draft revision as revised legislation only if it is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(7) (src:157)
GIVEN `the Board is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 15(7): certification is open to the Board` `the Board is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1` MEANS
    `the Board is satisfied that the changes made are within the powers set out in Article 14 or Schedule 1`
